# Line endings, decided by the repository rather than by each contributor's
# `core.autocrlf` setting.
#
# CI runs on Ubuntu and executes the shell steps in .github/workflows plus the
# Node scripts in scripts/. A CRLF that reached those would break them in ways
# that look nothing like a line-ending problem, and `scripts/check-encoding.mjs`
# exists because this project has already lost time to exactly that class of bug.

# Normalise every text file to LF inside the repository. Git decides what is
# text by inspection; the explicit rules below cover the cases worth pinning.
* text=auto

# Executed by tooling — LF even when checked out on Windows.
*.sh   text eol=lf
*.mjs  text eol=lf
*.yml  text eol=lf
*.yaml text eol=lf
*.sql  text eol=lf

# Source and content.
*.ts    text
*.tsx   text
*.json  text
*.md    text
*.css   text
*.svg   text
*.toml  text
*.prisma text

# Never transformed: a substituted byte here is a corrupted file, not a diff.
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif  binary
*.ico  binary
*.webp binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.pdf  binary
